## Validation requirements

Release-verifier tests will cover valid, unsigned, altered file, altered manifest, altered signature, unknown/revoked key, payload mismatch, malformed data, unsupported policy, and key rollover. Backend tests will cover role/transition rules, append-only event ordering, revision conflict, gate completeness, evidence/hash mismatch, and quarantine. Explorer tests will cover schema/lineage/uncertainty gaps, status filtering, comparison mismatch, and no-data/unavailable states. Dashboard tests will be component, interaction, accessibility, desktop/mobile, and fail-closed feed tests. Product tests will ask users to state what was checked, what remains unknown, and their next evidence action.

## Required decisions before production-facing execution

Core implementation can begin with test keys, metadata-only ingestion, and a steward-reviewed MVP. Before real release signing or external-user rollout, the program needs: **(1)** a named release-key/rollover owner, and **(2)** a choice between internal-steward-only review and independently authenticated external submitters. A quantitative keyword workbook additionally needs target country/worldwide scope and SEO data source. These decisions do not block the planned comparison, local signing fixtures, review-schema, or reality-trace work.

